# Step 4 Analysis

## 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 79 high-confidence hits with strong effects on IFNG production. Key observations: (1) Negative regulators dominate the hits (CD3D, ZAP70, VAV1, LCP2 show -3 to -4 fold changes), suggesting TCR signaling suppression increases IFNG; (2) Positive hits include epigenetic regulators (BRD4, BRD9), ubiquitin machinery (UBE2F, UBE2L3), and metabolic genes (TSC1/2, CTPS1); (3) The signal-to-noise ratio is excellent—hit scores are 5-10x larger than background genes. To optimize the next round, I should prioritize: genes functionally connected to validated hits, untested components of pathways already implicated (TCR, JAK-STAT, NF-κB), and epigenetic/metabolic regulators that co-cluster with strong hits.

## 2. Research Plan

