# 1. Reflection

The screening has identified 79 high-impact hits with strong effect sizes, revealing key regulatory pathways in IFNG production. Notable patterns include: (1) negative regulators like TBX21, ZAP70, VAV1, CD3D, CD3E showing strong suppression of IFNG when perturbed, suggesting these are essential positive regulators; (2) positive hits like MAP4K1, CBLB, NFKB2, TSC1 that enhance IFNG when knocked out, indicating they normally suppress it; (3) enrichment in T-cell signaling (CD4, CD28, LCK, ZAP70, PLCG1), JAK-STAT pathway (JAK1, JAK3, STAT3), and NF-κB signaling (IKBKB, CHUK, RELA). The next round should systematically test genes in proximal signaling nodes, epigenetic regulators, and cytokine signaling components that are mechanistically connected to validated hits but haven't been tested yet.

# 2. Research Plan

