# Step 4 Analysis

## 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 79 strong hits with substantial effect sizes (many |scores| > 0.4). Key observations: negative regulators of IFNG include CD3D/E/G (T cell receptor signaling), ZAP70, LCP2, VAV1, PLCG1 (TCR downstream), JAK1, STAT3, MAP3K7 (inflammatory signaling), and IKBKG/IKBKB (NF-κB). Positive regulators include MAP4K1, CBLB, BRD9, BRD4, NFKB2, PRKCH, and CTPS1. This reveals that IFNG production requires both TCR/costimulatory signals AND transcriptional/epigenetic machinery, but is suppressed by negative feedback (SOCS proteins, phosphatases). Next steps should focus on: (1) genes functionally related to identified hits, (2) understudied components of JAK-STAT and NF-κB pathways, (3) metabolic and epigenetic regulators, and (4) T cell activation/differentiation factors.

## 2. Research Plan

