# Step 4: CRISPR Screen for IFNG Regulators

## 1. Reflection
The screen has identified 79 hits with large effect sizes, revealing key signaling pathways regulating IFNG. Notable patterns emerge: (1) Strong negative hits include CD3D, ZAP70, VAV1, LCP2, PLCG1 (TCR signaling), CD28, PTPRC (T cell co-stimulation), and JAK1, TYK2-related pathway components; (2) Strong positive hits include MAP4K1, CBLB, NFKB2, TSC1 (likely negative regulators whose knockout increases IFNG); (3) The tested genes show modest effect sizes (range: -0.38 to +0.38), suggesting the high-impact genes remain undiscovered. To maximize the score, I should focus on: genes in the same pathways as strong hits, genes with known roles in Th1 differentiation and IFNG production, and genes that may directly or indirectly modulate the JAK-STAT, NF-κB, and TCR signaling axes.

## 2. Research Plan
