# Analysis of CRISPR Screen for IFNG Regulation

## 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 79 high-impact hits with substantial effect sizes (|score| > 0.4). Key observations: (1) Negative hits cluster around TCR/CD3 signaling (CD3D, CD3E, CD3G, ZAP70, LCP2, VAV1, PLCG1) and JAK-STAT pathway (JAK1, JAK3, STAT3), suggesting these suppress IFNG; (2) Positive hits include epigenetic regulators (BRD4, BRD9, CBLB, TSC1, NFKB2) and ubiquitin machinery (UBE2F, UBE2E1, UBE2L3); (3) The remaining ~18,800 untested genes likely include additional pathway regulators. Strategy: prioritize genes functionally connected to identified hits through pathway analysis, focusing on upstream regulators, co-factors, and parallel pathway components.

## 2. Research Plan

