# 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 79 strong hits with notable effects on IFNG production. Key observations include: (1) Strong negative regulators (JAK1, CD3D, ZAP70, VAV1, LCP2, PLCG1, CD28) suggest T cell receptor signaling is critical; (2) Strong positive regulators (MAP4K1, CBLB, NFKB2, TSC1, BRD9) point to immune activation pathways; (3) The presence of both JAK/STAT components and negative feedback (SOCS genes, DUSP genes) indicates pathway balance is important. The next round should focus on: genes in the top-hit pathways not yet tested (TCR signaling, NF-κB, MAPK cascades), co-factors of identified hits, and genes predicted to interact with the validated regulators.

# 2. Research Plan

