# Step 4 Analysis

## 1. Reflection
The screen has identified 79 high-impact hits with strong IFNG regulation signals. Key observations: (1) Strong negative regulators include CD3D, ZAP70, VAV1, CD3G, LCP2, PLCG1 (T-cell signaling), and JAK1, TBX21 (IFN-γ pathway components); (2) Strong positive regulators include MAP4K1, CBLB, NFKB2, TSC1, CTPS1 (immune signaling); (3) The data shows clear enrichment in TCR/BCR signaling, JAK/STAT pathway, NF-κB signaling, and chromatin remodeling. With ~18,800 genes untested and 128 slots available, I should prioritize genes functionally related to the validated hits while avoiding already-tested genes.

## 2. Research Plan
