# CRISPR Screen Analysis for IFNG Regulation

## 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 79 high-impact hits with strong effect sizes. Key observations: (1) CD3D, ZAP70, VAV1, and CD3G are strong negative regulators (scores < -3.6), suggesting TCR signaling suppresses IFNG; (2) MAP4K1 and CBLB are strong positive regulators (scores > 1.2), indicating they promote IFNG; (3) Several JAK-STAT pathway components (JAK1, JAK3, STAT3) are negative hits, suggesting context-dependent roles; (4) Epigenetic regulators (CREBBP, HDAC7, KDM1A) show mixed effects; (5) We have 128 slots available and have tested ~564 genes total, leaving ~18,375 untested genes. The strategy should focus on pathway extension and functional validation of biological networks connected to the hits.

## 2. Research Plan

